<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cleitus of Illyria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 335 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cleitus was an Illyrian king of the 4th century BCE, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bardylis">Bardylis</a>, whose realm lay on the north-western borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>. In 335 BCE he rose against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> and, with the Taulantian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glaukias">Glaukias</a>, held the fortress of Pelion. Alexander defeated them, and Cleitus burned the town and fled to Glaukias.</p></div>
